33:19.865 --> 33:22.607
Believe this shit? A girl that young?

33:24.135 --> 33:27.605
You know the sheriff has got a stake
in this place, too.

33:27.672 --> 33:29.208
Fucking Christ.

33:29.608 --> 33:31.986
"The King's children were marked.

33:32.277 --> 33:34.223
"They became his angels."

33:40.852 --> 33:43.799
The Yellow King, Carcosa.

33:44.689 --> 33:45.963
Nut job.

33:47.626 --> 33:49.572
Fried her brain on whatever she was on.

33:49.661 --> 33:52.574
Sounds like she didn't have much
to begin with.

33:52.664 --> 33:54.905
Well, it reads like fantasy.

33:57.302 --> 33:59.714
What if he was dosing her regular,

33:59.804 --> 34:04.651
and over a period of time, upping the dose
little by little without her knowing?

34:05.477 --> 34:10.756
We should stay out here today,
check around for johns, maybe knew her.

34:11.983 --> 34:13.428
Look at this.

34:16.421 --> 34:19.561
Oh, yeah. Man, a lot of these type places.

34:20.191 --> 34:22.728
Expect the ﬂock to canvass for them.

34:24.095 --> 34:27.235
You know, we should go there.
Could be the church everyone mentioned.

34:27.332 --> 34:30.108
Well, let's check around for johns
while we're out here

34:30.201 --> 34:32.511
and pick up the church on Monday.

34:35.674 --> 34:38.211
Most of your
stuffs still redacted.

34:38.710 --> 34:40.383
Now, what's Northshore?

34:43.014 --> 34:45.551
Northshore Psychiatric Hospital.

34:46.518 --> 34:50.193
Lubbock, Texas.
I spent four months there in '93.

34:50.889 --> 34:53.233
- You feel like talking about that?
- Well, sure.

34:54.059 --> 34:55.697
Who gives a shit?

35:00.699 --> 35:07.480
Sofia, my daughter,
she was on her tricycle in our driveway.

35:07.772 --> 35:08.944
Um...

35:15.213 --> 35:18.717
We lived on... We were in a
little bend in the road, and...

35:21.386 --> 35:23.059
They said that...

35:28.226 --> 35:30.069
Anyway, afterwards, uh,

35:31.763 --> 35:34.744
Claire and I turned on
each other, you know.

35:35.567 --> 35:38.810
We... We resented each other
for being alive, you know.

35:43.441 --> 35:47.583
I transferred from Robbery to Narco.

35:49.414 --> 35:51.917
Started hitting it, you know, 2417.

35:52.684 --> 35:54.686
Street rips, knocking down doors.

35:54.786 --> 35:58.165
Within three months I was
ripping off couriers

35:58.256 --> 36:02.295
or ending up in a Ramada Inn
with a couple of fucking eight-balls.

36:02.460 --> 36:03.768
Oh, yeah.

36:07.265 --> 36:09.609
Somewhere in there Claire left,

36:11.670 --> 36:15.049
and somewhere in there
I emptied a .9 into a crankhead

36:15.140 --> 36:18.280
for injecting his infant
daughter with crystal.

36:19.944 --> 36:22.322
Said he was trying to purify her.

36:24.816 --> 36:27.695
State Attorney gave me one chance
to stay out of jail.

36:27.786 --> 36:32.633
He said, "You can keep your profile,
but we wanna make you our wildman junkie."

36:33.191 --> 36:36.297
So they did.
They made me a floater, like a trick.

36:36.361 --> 36:40.468
You know, any agency or department
needed a deep undercover narco,

36:40.632 --> 36:42.009
they got me.

36:42.067 --> 36:45.139
And there was no fucking expiration date,
baby.

36:46.171 --> 36:48.981
And they kept you out there for four years?

36:49.040 --> 36:50.417
Mmm-hmm.

36:50.508 --> 36:55.719
In February of '93, I killed three
cartel men at the Port of Houston.

36:56.715 --> 36:59.753
I took three .25s in the side

36:59.851 --> 37:03.924
and ended up at Northshore
Psychiatric Hospital in Lubbock, Texas.

37:04.989 --> 37:07.435
Which is kind of funny in its own right.

37:07.525 --> 37:10.028
Psych ward being in Lubbock' Texas.

37:10.195 --> 37:12.004
You ever been there?

37:12.263 --> 37:14.607
They offered me a psych pension.

37:14.999 --> 37:16.535
Jackpot, right?

37:17.335 --> 37:21.181
I said no.
I said, "Put me on Homicide somewhere."

37:21.873 --> 37:24.581
By then, I was owed quite a few favors,

37:24.876 --> 37:27.914
and, uh, Louisiana was what they had.

37:33.218 --> 37:36.791
Yeah, for a long time after, I...
I didn't really sleep.

37:38.456 --> 37:42.370
Nightmares, PTSD,
exhausted nerves, whatever.

38:15.927 --> 38:17.065
Yeah.

38:19.898 --> 38:21.343
Why Homicide?

38:23.434 --> 38:25.675
Oh, something I saw at Northshore.

38:27.338 --> 38:29.249
Quote from Corinthians.

38:33.111 --> 38:37.082
"The body is not one member, but many.

38:38.983 --> 38:41.759
"Now are they many,

38:43.321 --> 38:44.994
"but of one body."

38:46.090 --> 38:47.763
What's that mean, though?

38:49.494 --> 38:52.304
I was just trying to stay
a part of the body now.

38:53.698 --> 38:55.769
The fishing pole's not working.

38:55.834 --> 38:57.836
- Just ask Grandpa.
- No.

38:58.536 --> 39:01.142
- Yeah.
- Grandpa, I can't tell if it's working.

39:01.206 --> 39:04.119
You'll know, honey. It'll yank at you hard.

39:04.442 --> 39:06.820
- Okay.
- Why don't you...

39:06.878 --> 39:09.381
How's that case going? The big one?

39:11.950 --> 39:13.725
Working it, you know.

39:16.688 --> 39:19.294
Things like that didn't happen these pans
when I was young.

39:19.357 --> 39:21.894
People said "ma'am" and "sir"

39:21.993 --> 39:23.995
Families stayed together.

39:25.230 --> 39:27.471
Yeah, that's how it was, huh?

39:28.800 --> 39:30.473
Not all the time.

39:31.169 --> 39:33.046
There was more dignity.

39:33.137 --> 39:36.983
Everyone wasn't out in the street,
yelling about their rights.

39:37.575 --> 39:42.490
Well, if things were so great,
they never would have changed.

39:42.981 --> 39:43.982
Hmm.

39:44.048 --> 39:45.550
Nothing is going on.

39:45.650 --> 39:48.995
I'm just saying, if there's a problem,
you can talk to me. You know that.

39:49.053 --> 39:51.556
If I have a problem with someone,
I talk to them, Ma.

39:51.656 --> 39:53.727
Well, you should be able lo talk to me.

39:53.825 --> 39:56.829
I know what it's like
to be married to a man.

39:57.061 --> 39:59.041
You think they're all the same, huh?

39:59.864 --> 40:03.334
I don't know why you're so rude to me. If
you're frustrated, don't take it out on me.

40:04.102 --> 40:06.241
I think that you need
to get your cable fixed

40:06.337 --> 40:08.715
and stop confusing me
with your soap operas.

40:08.773 --> 40:11.185
Well, you beat up on
what you can't control.

40:11.776 --> 40:13.847
Makes it bad for everybody else.

40:14.345 --> 40:16.586
- I don't know how.
- I don't care. Just try.

40:16.681 --> 40:18.524
- You do it.
- I can't.

40:19.017 --> 40:20.553
You have smaller fingers.

40:20.618 --> 40:22.291
Macie, just do it.

40:24.522 --> 40:27.264
So, you're telling me
the world isn't getting worse?

40:27.358 --> 40:32.706
I've seen kids today, all in black,
wearing makeup, shit on their faces.

40:33.097 --> 40:34.735
Even/thing's sex.

40:35.266 --> 40:36.540
Clinton.

40:38.036 --> 40:40.107
You know, throughout history,

40:40.204 --> 40:43.378
I bet every old man
probably said the same thing.

40:43.808 --> 40:46.812
And old men die,
and the world keeps spinning.

40:50.048 --> 40:52.654
- Honey, I got this lead...
- How are the girls?

40:53.284 --> 40:57.096
I got this lead I wanted to check up on.
I told you about it.

40:57.722 --> 41:02.137
- Maybe your dad could bring you back.
- No. You didn't tell me anything about it.

41:02.226 --> 41:04.069
This is a family day.

41:04.729 --> 41:07.232
I did tell you about it. I mentioned it.

41:08.299 --> 41:09.972
It's the new case.

41:14.272 --> 41:16.479
Okay, well, how about
we all head back, then?

41:16.574 --> 41:19.316
Hmm. All right, sweetheart.

41:20.244 --> 41:21.814
Come on! Let's go!

41:21.913 --> 41:23.586
Our lines tangled.

41:23.781 --> 41:25.658
- Just paddle in.
- Okay.

41:26.184 --> 41:27.288
Told you!

41:28.186 --> 41:30.530
- Thanks for the lovely afternoon.
- Oh.

41:33.291 --> 41:34.634
Thank you.

42:00.518 --> 42:01.519
Afternoon, sir.

42:01.953 --> 42:04.559
- How you doing today, Officer'?
- I have a question for you.

42:04.655 --> 42:06.635
You ever seen this girl?

42:06.958 --> 42:09.234
- You never seen her before?
- Never before.

42:09.327 --> 42:10.362
How about you?

42:36.654 --> 42:37.894
Question.

42:37.989 --> 42:40.401
I'm looking for this young lady.
Do you recognize her?

42:41.692 --> 42:43.433
I might need a memory jog.

42:43.728 --> 42:45.708
Dora. Young blonde?

42:46.330 --> 42:48.503
Dora. Dora, Dora, Dora, Dora.

42:49.167 --> 42:50.168
Dora.

42:50.601 --> 42:54.276
Have any guys come around lately
looking for anything more than a good time?

42:54.405 --> 42:57.113
You might be able to remember
for a little more money?

42:57.208 --> 42:59.017
- I might.
- You might?

43:07.618 --> 43:10.360
Years, we've been through this.

43:11.889 --> 43:15.268
Sweetheart, listen to me.
There is nowhere else I want to be.

43:17.295 --> 43:18.856
I wonder if you even know you're lying.

43:19.430 --> 43:20.636
Oh, come on!

43:20.731 --> 43:21.732
Shh.

43:22.600 --> 43:27.606
Bad enough the shit I got to wade through
on a daily basis,

43:27.705 --> 43:30.049
bring me this "feel bad for me" crap

43:30.608 --> 43:32.884
when I work 30 hours straight

43:32.977 --> 43:36.550
and spent the weekend
listening to your dad's bullshit.

43:37.048 --> 43:42.498
I come home, the one place where
there's supposed to be peace and calm,

43:42.587 --> 43:44.507
- and you throw this shit...
- Who told you that?

43:45.590 --> 43:48.002
It's not always that way.
It's not supposed to be.

43:48.092 --> 43:51.232
It's supposed to be what I want.
It's supposed to help me.

43:51.295 --> 43:54.276
We do help you! All the goddamn time!

43:58.569 --> 44:01.140
Okay, well, what do you want me to say?

44:01.239 --> 44:04.777
You want me to talk about the woman,
had antlers?

44:04.842 --> 44:07.652
Do you want me to tell you
about the kids disappearing,

44:07.745 --> 44:11.625
